:"","namespace":"","id":"0","width":256,"height":512,"uv_width":256,"uv_height":512,"particle":false,"use_as_default":true,"layers_enabled":false,"sync_to_project":"","render_mode":"default","render_sides":"auto","frame_time":1,"frame_order_type":"loop","frame_order":"","frame_interpolate":false,"visible":true,"internal":true,"saved":true,"uuid":"717e8669-78f9-5a07-a906-3cec3de4117b","relative_path":"farmhouse_t2.png","source":"data:image/png;base64,"}],"animations":[],"description":"# farmhouse_t2\n\nFarmhouse tier 2: a timber-frame house, plastered panels between dark posts, shingled roof.\n\n- Footprint: 6 x 5 columns (96 x 80 units, 2.70 x 2.25 m), centred on the origin, front (door side) faces -Z.\n- Finished bounds: x -55..46, y 0..138, z -34..34 units.\n- Texture: 256 x 512, 1 px per unit, square pixels, nearest filtering. Every visible face has its own texture region painted with its material at world position (seams line up across faces); identical faces share a region; construction and ruined pieces map into the region of the face they were cut from. No cube is cut to fit the texture.\n- Cubes: finished 81, construction_0 45, construction_33 55, construction_66 69, ruined 46 (6 rotated: roof slabs and a few leaning props).\n\n## Hit box\n\n- 80 x 130 x 60 centred at the origin\n\n## State group sets (children of `root`; show exactly one)\n\n- `finished`: the finished building (visible by default).\n- `construction_0`, `construction_33`, `construction_66`: build progress at 0 %, 33 % and 66 % (staked outline and scaffold, then walls rising inside scaffold, then full frame with roof rafters).\n- `ruined`: collapsed shell, broken walls, rubble, fallen roof (use with `_damaged.png`, or `_abandoned.png` for F7 abandoned buildings).\n- `farmhouse_t2_damaged.png`: damaged texture (scorch, holes, cracks) for the same UVs; works on every group set.\n- `farmhouse_t2_abandoned.png`: abandoned look (damage plus moss, faded cloth, cold fires) = `abandoned_farmhouse_t2` together with the `ruined` set or the finished set.\n\n## Attachment and effect points (empty groups)\n\n- `slot_door` at (0, 0, -39)\n- `fx_smoke` at (28, 139, 12)\n"}